---
description: Corsa SDK coding conventions — use CorsaClient, proper auth format, referenceId patterns
alwaysApply: false
globs: "**/*.ts"
---

- Use `CorsaClient` from `@corsa-labs/sdk` — `ComplianceClient` is deprecated
- Use `RiskDto.level` for risk levels — `ClientRiskDto` is stale / does not exist in the SDK exports
- Authentication format: `Bearer <API_TOKEN>:<API_SECRET>` in the `Authorization` header
- Provide `referenceId` (your internal system ID) when creating entities — you can use either `referenceId` or Corsa's generated `id` in subsequent calls
- Configure auth via the constructor `HEADERS` option — `TOKEN` only sets `Bearer <value>` which doesn't support Corsa's `TOKEN:SECRET` compound format
- Base URLs: US `https://api.corsa.finance`, EU `https://api.eu.corsa.finance`
- Rate limit: 500 requests per 60 seconds per user — respect `Retry-After` header on 429
- Creation endpoints support `upsert=true` to update-or-create by `referenceId`
